From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 18:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bluestore: initialize tracer + add read-path spans

ceph-20.1.1-bluestore-local-tracer.patch (PATCH 09/10) introduced a
new tracing::bluestore::tracer global to make the os library
self-contained (so ceph-bluestore-tool can link without OSD
symbols), and redirected the two existing call sites in BlueStore.cc
(queue_transactions, txc_aio_wait) from tracing::osd::tracer to the
new tracer. That fixed the link error but never wired an exporter
to the bluestore tracer, so those spans have been silently dropping
since the patch landed. nm shows the symbol is in /usr/bin/ceph-osd
but its internal OTLP provider is null, and add_span returns a
no-op span.

Fix by initializing the bluestore tracer alongside the osd tracer
in OSD::init(). Each Tracer instance gets its own provider with its
own resource (service.name=bluestore), so bluestore spans show up
as a distinct service in Tempo and contribute their own
traces_spanmetrics_* series.

Also add a "bluestore_read" span at the entry of BlueStore::read()
to give GET-path observability. The librados public API has no
IoCtx::operate(ObjectReadOperation*, ..., jspan_context*) overload,
so RGW GET requests can't carry trace context down to the OSD/store.
Until that's fixed, bluestore_read spans are orphan traces — they
still emit Prometheus span metrics (latency histograms per OSD) and
are searchable in Tempo, just not linked under the parent RGW GET
trace. Tagging offset/length as span attributes so TraceQL can
filter by request size.

Two known follow-ups:
  * Add IoCtx::operate / aio_operate overloads accepting
    jspan_context* for ObjectReadOperation, thread through Objecter
    and MOSDOp, so reads carry trace context end-to-end.
  * Add an _do_read child span inside BlueStore::read to split
    onode-load latency from the actual data read.

Signed-off-by: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
---
 src/osd/OSD.cc                 | 2 ++
 src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc  | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/osd/OSD.cc b/src/osd/OSD.cc
--- a/src/osd/OSD.cc
+++ b/src/osd/OSD.cc
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@
 #include "os/ObjectStore.h"

 #include "os/FuseStore.h"
+#include "os/bluestore/bluestore_tracer.h"

 #include "PrimaryLogPG.h"

@@ -3744,6 +3745,7 @@ int OSD::init()
   if (is_stopping())
     return 0;
   tracing::osd::tracer.init(cct, "osd", std::to_string(whoami));
+  tracing::bluestore::tracer.init(cct, "bluestore", std::to_string(whoami));
   tick_timer.init();
   tick_timer_without_osd_lock.init();
   service.recovery_request_timer.init();
diff --git a/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc b/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc
--- a/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc
+++ b/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc
@@ -12449,6 +12449,12 @@ int BlueStore::read(
   bufferlist& bl,
   uint32_t op_flags)
 {
+  auto read_span = tracing::bluestore::tracer.start_trace("bluestore_read");
+  if (read_span->IsRecording()) {
+    read_span->SetAttribute("offset", (int64_t)offset);
+    read_span->SetAttribute("length", (int64_t)length);
+    read_span->SetAttribute("op_flags", (int64_t)op_flags);
+  }
   auto start = mono_clock::now();
   Collection *c = static_cast<Collection *>(c_.get());
   const coll_t &cid = c->get_cid();
